  "notes": "From the name of the search engine Google, turned into a godan る-verb: ググった, ググって, ググれば. Usually written ググる, katakana with a hiragana ending; ぐぐる also occurs.\n\nUSAGE:\nInformal; common in speech, chat and social media. It is used for any web search, not only with Google, as \"to google\" is in English.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- ググってみる: to try googling it\n- ググれば⟦{分|わ}かる→分かる：00463_wakaru⟧: you can find it by googling\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- ⟦{検索|けんさく}→検索：04729_kensaku⟧⟦する→する：00392_suru⟧: to search — the neutral word, fine in any register",
